External knowledge that might be helpful: 
# Details of bike share trips

- trip ID
- duration (s)
- start date
- start station name
  - Not null
- route : `start_station_name` - `end_station_name` (there is " - " between two strings of names)
- bike number
- subscriber type
- member birth year
  - Not null
- age := current year - birth year
  - Not null
- age class
  - age < 40 : 'Young (<40 Y.O)'
  - 40 <= age <= 60 : 'Adult (40-60 Y.O)'
  - age > 60 : 'Senior Adult (>60 Y.O)'
- member gender
  - Not null
- region name
The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS': {'SAN_FRANCISCO_311': ['_311_SERVICE_REQUESTS'], 'SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE': ['BIKESHARE_STATION_STATUS', 'BIKESHARE_REGIONS', 'BIKESHARE_STATION_INFO', 'BIKESHARE_TRIPS'], 'SAN_FRANCISCO_FILM_LOCATIONS': ['FILM_LOCATIONS'], 'SAN_FRANCISCO_NEIGHBORHOODS': ['BOUNDARIES'], 'SAN_FRANCISCO_SFFD_SERVICE_CALLS': ['SFFD_SERVICE_CALLS'], 'SAN_FRANCISCO_SFPD_INCIDENTS': ['SFPD_INCIDENTS'], 'SAN_FRANCISCO_TRANSIT_MUNI': ['CALENDAR', 'FARES', 'SHAPES', 'VEHICLE_MONITORING', 'STOPS', 'STOP_TIMES', 'TRIPS', 'ROUTES', 'STOP_MONITORING'], 'SAN_FRANCISCO_TREES': ['STREET_TREES']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their possible roles  
• "trip_id": uniquely identify each ride (output).  
• "duration_sec": trip length in seconds – used for ranking and output.  
• "start_date": micro‑seconds POSIX timestamp – filter 2017‑07‑01 → 2017‑12‑31 (inclusive).  
• "start_station_name": starting station; must be NOT NULL, appears in output.  
• "end_station_name": build the “route” string start → end.  
• "start_station_id": key to look‑up region.  
• "end_station_id": not needed except for the “route” label.  
• "subscriber_type": rider category – output.  
• "member_birth_year": birth year – compute age; exclude NULL.  
• "member_gender": gender – exclude NULL; output.  
• "bike_number": bicycle used – output.  

Additional tables / columns for region look‑up  
• BIKESHARE_STATION_INFO."station_id": join key (cast to text).  
• BIKESHARE_STATION_INFO."region_id": foreign key to region.  
• BIKESHARE_REGIONS."region_id": join key.  
• BIKESHARE_REGIONS."name": region name – output.  

Typical conditions  
1. "start_date" BETWEEN 1498867200000000 AND 1514764799000000  (July 1 → Dec 31 2017, epoch µs).  
2. "start_station_name" IS NOT NULL AND "member_birth_year" IS NOT NULL AND "member_gender" IS NOT NULL.  

Age & classification (using 2024 as “current” year here)  
• age = 2024 – "member_birth_year"  
• CASE WHEN age < 40 THEN 'Young (<40 Y.O)'  
     WHEN age BETWEEN 40 AND 60 THEN 'Adult (40‑60 Y.O)'  
     ELSE 'Senior Adult (>60 Y.O)' END AS age_class  

Below are 10 exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20 rows each) that gradually build to the final result.  
(All identifiers are wrapped in double quotes; adjust boundaries/year if needed.)

```sql
-- 1. Quick peek at the raw trips table
SELECT
  "trip_id",
  "duration_sec",
  "start_date",
  "start_station_name",
  "end_station_name"
FROM SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_TRIPS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Check the micro‑second epoch values around July 2017
SELECT DISTINCT
  "start_date"
FROM SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_TRIPS
WHERE "start_date" BETWEEN 1498867200000000 AND 1498868200000000
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Filter the 2017‑H2 window and keep only required non‑NULL columns
SELECT
  "trip_id",
  "duration_sec",
  "start_date",
  "start_station_name",
  "end_station_name",
  "member_birth_year",
  "member_gender"
FROM SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_TRIPS
WHERE "start_date" BETWEEN 1498867200000000 AND 1514764799000000
  AND "start_station_name" IS NOT NULL
  AND "member_birth_year" IS NOT NULL
  AND "member_gender" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Create the “route” field (start → end)
SELECT
  "trip_id",
  "duration_sec",
  "start_station_name" || ' - ' || "end_station_name" AS "route"
FROM SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_TRIPS
WHERE "start_date" BETWEEN 1498867200000000 AND 1514764799000000
  AND "start_station_name" IS NOT NULL
  AND "member_birth_year" IS NOT NULL
  AND "member_gender" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Compute rider's age based on birth year (using 2024 as current year)
SELECT
  "trip_id",
  2024 - "member_birth_year" AS "age"
FROM SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_TRIPS
WHERE "member_birth_year" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Add age classification buckets
SELECT
  "trip_id",
  2024 - "member_birth_year" AS "age",
  CASE
    WHEN 2024 - "member_birth_year" < 40 THEN 'Young (<40 Y.O)'
    WHEN 2024 - "member_birth_year" BETWEEN 40 AND 60 THEN 'Adult (40-60 Y.O)'
    ELSE 'Senior Adult (>60 Y.O)'
  END AS "age_class"
FROM SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_TRIPS
WHERE "member_birth_year" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Look up the region_id of a start station
SELECT
  t."start_station_id",
  i."region_id"
FROM SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_TRIPS t
JOIN SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_STATION_INFO i
      ON CAST(t."start_station_id" AS TEXT) = i."station_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Convert region_id to the public region name
SELECT
  i."station_id",
  r."name" AS "region_name"
FROM SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_STATION_INFO i
JOIN SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_REGIONS r
      ON i."region_id" = r."region_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Combine trips with region name and prepared fields, still un‑ranked
SELECT
  t."trip_id",
  t."duration_sec",
  t."start_date",
  t."start_station_name",
  t."end_station_name",
  t."bike_number",
  t."subscriber_type",
  t."member_birth_year",
  2024 - t."member_birth_year" AS "age",
  CASE
    WHEN 2024 - t."member_birth_year" < 40 THEN 'Young (<40 Y.O)'
    WHEN 2024 - t."member_birth_year" BETWEEN 40 AND 60 THEN 'Adult (40-60 Y.O)'
    ELSE 'Senior Adult (>60 Y.O)'
  END AS "age_class",
  t."member_gender",
  r."name" AS "region_name"
FROM SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_TRIPS t
JOIN SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_STATION_INFO i
      ON CAST(t."start_station_id" AS TEXT) = i."station_id"
JOIN SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_REGIONS r
      ON i."region_id" = r."region_id"
WHERE t."start_date" BETWEEN 1498867200000000 AND 1514764799000000
  AND t."start_station_name" IS NOT NULL
  AND t."member_birth_year" IS NOT NULL
  AND t."member_gender" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final query: Top‑5 longest trips in requested window with all requested fields
SELECT
  t."trip_id",
  t."duration_sec",
  t."start_date",
  t."start_station_name",
  t."start_station_name" || ' - ' || t."end_station_name" AS "route",
  t."bike_number",
  t."subscriber_type",
  t."member_birth_year",
  2024 - t."member_birth_year" AS "age",
  CASE
    WHEN 2024 - t."member_birth_year" < 40 THEN 'Young (<40 Y.O)'
    WHEN 2024 - t."member_birth_year" BETWEEN 40 AND 60 THEN 'Adult (40-60 Y.O)'
    ELSE 'Senior Adult (>60 Y.O)'
  END AS "age_class",
  t."member_gender",
  r."name" AS "region_name"
FROM SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_TRIPS t
JOIN SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_STATION_INFO i
      ON CAST(t."start_station_id" AS TEXT) = i."station_id"
JOIN SAN_FRANCISCO_PLUS.SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_REGIONS r
      ON i."region_id" = r."region_id"
WHERE t."start_date" BETWEEN 1498867200000000 AND 1514764799000000
  AND t."start_station_name" IS NOT NULL
  AND t."member_birth_year" IS NOT NULL
  AND t."member_gender" IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY t."duration_sec" DESC
LIMIT 5;
```
